# Astra-CISO v3.0 — Decision Loop (release/v3-decision-loop)
# Architecture context for AI-assisted development

## Value (do not ship features that fail this)
Astra is where security decisions get made, evidenced, and remembered.
1. Does this create, evidence, or close a decision?
2. Is the data real (or clearly empty), never silently mocked?
3. Can the CISO show an auditor what happened?
4. Same inputs + same skill version → same output (or an explicit labeled draft)?

Skills compute. LLM drafts only. OpenNeko watches and approval-gates — it does not own domain truth.

## Platform Overview
- CISO decision loop on ZTAIP (Zero Trust AI Platform)
- Next.js 16, React 19, TypeScript 5, Prisma 7, Postgres 16
- Dark hacker theme (Bloomberg Terminal aesthetic) — never use light backgrounds
- Version: 3.0.0-decision.2 on branch release/v3-decision-loop

## Skills (src/lib/skills/)
- caiq.match@1.0.0 — deterministic KB match, no I/O, golden tests required
- caiq.score@1.0.0 — coverage from match hits
- caiq.draft@1.0.0 — LLM envelope only (source: ai_draft, cannot close a decision)
- risk.fiveByFive@1.0.0 — likelihood × impact bands
- evidence.expiry@1.0.0 — expiresAt vs asOf (clock is an input)
- vendor.goNoGo@1.0.0 — score + last Shodan snapshot vs appetite
- tabletop.score@1.0.0 — exercise grade from stored session decisions
- intel.correlate@1.0.0 — snapshot IOCs ∩ vendor domains / attack-surface hosts
- playbook.nextStep@1.0.0 — next incomplete Playbook checkbox
- Skill runs persist to SkillRun (inputHash, skillVersion, outputJson)
- Integration fetches persist to Observation (append-only). Never return MOCK intel.
- OpenNeko watchers call POST /api/internal/watchers/tick (x-astra-internal-secret)
- Approvals dual-write Approval + AuditLog (POST /api/internal/approvals)

## Modules (product surface)
Command Center, Decision Center, Strategy & OKRs, Governance & Risk, Vendor Risk, Incidents, Exercises, Threat Intel, Integrations, Settings, Help
AppSec and Roadmap fail the value test — hidden from nav.
If a screen does not create, evidence, or close a decision, hide it or delete it.

## Architecture Patterns
- ZTAIP: Zero Trust AI Platform — never trust, always verify
- Circuit Breaker: CLOSED → OPEN → HALF_OPEN per AI provider and intel API
- Dynamic Autonomy Router: AUTONOMOUS / SUPERVISED / MANUAL (default SUPERVISED)
- Immutable Audit Fabric: append-only AuditLog, never update/delete
- Deterministic skills + Observation snapshots

## AI Providers (multi-provider)
- Anthropic Claude, Google Gemini, Ollama (local)
- Always use circuit breaker per provider
- AI Economics: track tokens, cost, queries
- LLM output is a draft (source: ai_draft), never canonical without human approve

## Intelligence Module Patterns
### API Clients (src/lib/intelligence/clients/)
- All clients use circuit breaker pattern
- Persist snapshots via Observation (TTL: Shodan host 24h, search 1h)
- On failure: last Observation or empty — NEVER mock IOCs

### Shodan
- Rate limit: 1 request/second (free tier)
- Cache: host lookups 24h, search 1h (Observation table)
- All lookups logged to audit trail

### Abuse.ch
- ThreatFox: JSON POST to threatfox-api.abuse.ch
- URLhaus: Form-encoded POST to urlhaus-api.abuse.ch (NOT JSON)
- MalwareBazaar: JSON POST to mb-api.abuse.ch
- No API key needed for any Abuse.ch service

### Data Layers (World Monitor)
- Static layers: load from src/data/intelligence/*.json (always available)
- API-fed layers: show "Configure in Settings" if key missing
- All layers toggleable in LayerControlPanel

## Dark Theme Colors
- Background: #050508
- Card BG: rgba(8,12,24,0.85)
- Card Border: rgba(56,189,248,0.06)
- Primary accent: #38bdf8
- Success: #4ade80
- Warning: #fbbf24
- Critical: #ef4444

## Typography
- JetBrains Mono — numbers, metrics, KPIs (bold, colored)
- DM Sans — labels, descriptions, body text

## Component Organization
- src/components/command/ — Command Center widgets
- src/components/intelligence/ — Intelligence components
- src/components/intelligence/world-monitor/ — World Monitor map components
- src/lib/skills/ — deterministic skill runtime

## Code Conventions
- TypeScript strict mode, no `any` types
- Zod validation at all API boundaries
- React Server Components by default, 'use client' only when needed
- Prisma for all persistent data (never localStorage for business data)
- Zustand for UI state only (sidebar collapse, theme, active tab)
- @/ path alias for imports

## Database
- Postgres 16 via Prisma 7 (`@prisma/adapter-pg`). GraphJin / OpenNeko read the same DB.
- Key models: KnowledgeEntry, Observation, SkillRun, Approval, AuditLog, AttackSurfaceScan

## Deleted Features (DO NOT reference or recreate)
- Wargames module (replaced by Tabletop Exercises)
- Budget module
- Infrastructure placeholder
- Privacy placeholder
- Network telemetry widget
- OpenClaw agent (replaced by native AI)
- Light/purple theme (replaced by dark hacker theme)
- Docker-based threat intel stack (replaced by cloud APIs)
- Silent MOCK_* intel fallbacks (v3: empty or last Observation)
